&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1648&quot;&gt;While candidates in the listed location(s) are encouraged for this role, candidates in other locations will be considered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Databricks continues to grow both organically and through strategic acquisitions. To support our scale, we are elevating our People M&amp;amp;A engine to handle high-volume, and complex global deals. As a player-coach for this function, you will lead the strategic vision, hands-on execution, and continuous evolution of our global People M&amp;amp;A&amp;nbsp; function. Reporting to the Director of People Programs (Global Mobility, M&amp;amp;A, Compliance), you will bridge Corporate Development, People Leadership, and functional business teams to orchestrate end-to-end deal lifecycles—from due diligence through Day 1 execution and multi-year post-merger integration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a strategic builder who blends high-level vision with rigorous execution and a &quot;doer&quot; mentality. You will lead cross-functional deal teams, build scalable operational frameworks, manage senior executive stakeholders, and ensure every acquired employee experiences a world-class transition into Databricks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2006&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The impact you will have: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Deal Leadership &amp;amp; Due Diligence:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the primary People executive on M&amp;amp;A deals. Drive holistic due diligence, organizational design alignment, retention strategies, deal risk mitigation, and employment law strategy globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal Execution &amp;amp; Post-Merger Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and execute comprehensive integration strategies across Culture, Talent Acquisition, Total Rewards, People Operations, and Systems, balancing aggressive timeline targets with employee experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;M&amp;amp;A Platform &amp;amp; Playbook Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Architect and mature the enterprise People M&amp;amp;A Playbook, establishing standardized governance, automation roadmaps, and data-integrity frameworks with People Tech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Stakeholder Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with CorpDev, Legal, Finance, and Business Unit Leaders to present People diligence findings, synergy plans, and integration roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Functional Governance &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead cross-functional People workstreams (TA, Benefits, Total Rewards, Global Mobility, People Partners) to ensure seamless alignment, resource allocation, and program execution across deal phases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of progressive HR/People Operations experience, with 8+ years focused directly on leading end-to-end global M&amp;amp;A deals in high-growth tech environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of managing M&amp;amp;A programs across the full deal lifecycle: Due Diligence, Deal Structuring, Day 1 readiness, and Post-Merger Integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence with demonstrated ability to influence Founders/C-suite stakeholders, CorpDev leaders, and business executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep technical understanding of global People workflows, international employment law, compensation architecture, and system integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic builder mindset capable of operating at high altitude while maintaining rigor over deal execution and complex operational mechanics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
